## SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

## Build artifacts
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
Tests/ElectronFixture/node_modules/

## Rust plugin build output. Plugins are hermetic standalone crates whose
## committed Cargo.lock lives at Plugins/<id>/Cargo.lock (not ignored); a
## bare cargo run without CARGO_TARGET_DIR=build/plugin-target creates a
## watched Plugins/<id>/target/ — keep it out of the index.
Plugins/*/target/
Plugins/*/flash-plugin-*
# The global gitignore drops *.lock; hermetic plugin crates commit theirs.
!Plugins/*/Cargo.lock

## Python bytecode (interpreted plugins + Scripts tooling)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

## Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

## Local config / scratch
karabiner.json.bak-*
*.bak-flash

## Browser captures from the fixture collector are real browsing sessions:
## they stay local and must never be committed.
Tests/BrowserSnapshots/snapshots/collected-*
Tests/BrowserSnapshots/allowlists/collected-*

## Stray empty top-level dirs left over from earlier dev workflows. Keeping
## them out of the index avoids accidental commits if they ever pick up content.
/home/
/cache/
/bin/
/config/
/share/

## Per-plugin data-dir litter: running a plugin binary by hand without
## FLASH_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR historically mkdir'd these inside the source tree.
Plugins/*/home/
Plugins/*/config/
Plugins/*/cache/
Plugins/*/share/
Plugins/*/bin/
examples/plugins/go-spotify/flash-plugin-go-spotify
